WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.012
The doctrine is simple to state.

2
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:06.032
A net-new asset is governed from
the moment it first powers on:

3
00:00:06.032 --> 00:00:09.488
by Intune for endpoints, and
by Azure Arc for servers.

4
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:13.748
There is no state where it joins
on-premises Active Directory to wait for a

5
00:00:13.748 --> 00:00:18.147
migration, gets provisioned by
Configuration Manager and co-managed later,

6
00:00:18.147 --> 00:00:20.731
runs without an organizational assignment,

7
00:00:20.731 --> 00:00:24.013
or reaches production without
a compliance evaluation.

8
00:00:24.013 --> 00:00:27.553
Five pillars carry it, and
they're the program's doctrine,

9
00:00:27.553 --> 00:00:29.400
not Microsoft requirements.

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.100
No ungoverned device, ever;
quarantine is the safety valve.

11
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.304
Procurement is the first governance
step: the assignment is set when

12
00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:42.213
the purchase order is issued, the
way HR feeds user provisioning.

13
00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:43.549
Zero-touch only.

14
00:00:43.549 --> 00:00:45.660
One management plane per asset,

15
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:50.287
so no greenfield Configuration
Manager, Group Policy or hybrid join.

16
00:00:50.287 --> 00:00:53.996
And quarantine on failure: an
onboarding failure produces a

17
00:00:53.996 --> 00:00:58.075
quarantine entry and a ticket,
never a degraded production device.

18
00:00:58.075 --> 00:01:01.187
Every asset follows the same five phases.

19
00:01:01.187 --> 00:01:05.701
Procure, with the assignment validated
against the organizational registry.

20
00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.537
Pre-stage, where the
vendor record carries it.

21
00:01:08.537 --> 00:01:10.914
Position, where the governance pipeline

22
00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:13.500
commits a mapping keyed
on the serial number.

23
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.699
Note that phase 3 doesn't
pre-stage an Entra object;

24
00:01:16.699 --> 00:01:20.912
classic Autopilot creates that
automatically at registration,

25
00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:25.125
so phase 3 confirms the registration
carries the right group tag.

26
00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:26.962
Provision, zero-touch.

27
00:01:26.962 --> 00:01:28.050
And validate.

28
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:32.566
The assignment comes from the first
source that can supply it: procurement,

29
00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:35.844
then the vendor carrier, then
derivation from the user,

30
00:01:35.844 --> 00:01:38.612
and finally an explicit
unpositioned marker.

31
00:01:38.612 --> 00:01:41.974
A known nowhere is still
a value a rule can match.

32
00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:46.100
The latency target is fourteen
calendar days from purchase order,

33
00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.810
five for expedited orders.
